the battlefield, target opponent loses 3 life.', 'When Pilgrim of the Ages enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a basic Plains card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.\\n{6}: Return Pilgrim of the Ages from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Pit Keeper enters the battlefield, if you have four or more creature cards in your graveyard, you may return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', "When Plaguecrafter enters the battlefield, each player sacrifices a creature or planeswalker. Each player who can't discards a card.", "When Pridemalkin enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature you control.\\nEach creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it has trample. (They can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker they're attacking.)", 'When Priest of the Blood Rite enters the battlefield, create a 5/5 black Demon creature token with flying.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you lose 2 life.', "When Quakefoot Cyclops enters the battlefield, up to two target creatures can't block this turn.\\nCycling {1}{R} ({1}{R}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)\\nWhen you cycle Quakefoot Cyclops, target creature can't block this turn.", 'When Quarry Beetle enters the battlefield, you may return target land card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'When Rambunctious Mutt enters the battlefield, destroy target artifact or enchantment an opponent controls.', 'When Reclamation Sage enters the battlefield, you may destroy target artifact or enchantment.', 'When Returned Reveler dies, each player mills three cards.', 'When Rooting Moloch enters the battlefield, exile target card with a cycling ability from your graveyard. Until the end of your next turn, you may play that card.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'When Rosethorn Halberd enters the battlefield, attach it to target non-Human creature you control.\\nEquipped creature gets +2/+1.\\nEquip {5} ({5}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'When Runed Servitor dies, each player draws a card.', "When Sage's Row Savant enters the battlefield, scry 2.", 'When Savannah Sage enters the battlefield, you gain 2 life.', 'When Self-Assembler enters the battlefield, you may search your library for an Assembly-Worker creature card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'When Seller of Songbirds enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 white Bird creature token with flying.', 'When Skilled Animator enters the battlefield, target artifact you control becomes an artifact creature with base power and toughness 5/5 for as long as Skilled Animator remains on the battlefield.', "When Skullslither Worm enters the battlefield, each opponent discards a card. For each opponent who can't, put two +1/+1 counters on Skullslither Worm.", 'When Sling-Gang Lieutenant enters the battlefield, create two 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens.\\nSacrifice a Goblin: Target player loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.', 'When Smoldering Efreet dies, it deals 2 damage to you.', 'When Solemn Simulacrum enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.\\nWhen Solemn Simulacrum dies, you may draw a card.', 'When Soulcage Fiend dies, each player loses 3 life.', 'When Sparkmage Apprentice enters the battlefield, it deals 1 damage to any target.', 'When Spirited Companion enters the battlefield, draw a card.', "When Stitcher's Supplier enters the battlefield or dies, mill three cards.", "When Subterranean Scout enters the battlefield, target creature with power 2 or less can't be blocked this turn.", 'When Thraben Inspector enters the battlefield, investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")', 'When Uktabi Orangutan enters the battlefield, destroy target artifact.', 'When Viashino Pyromancer enters the battlefield, it deals 2 damage to target player or planeswalker.', 'When Volley Veteran enters the battlefield, it deals damage to target creature an opponent controls equal to the number of Goblins you control.', 'When Wailing Ghoul enters the battlefield, mill two cards.', "When Watertrap Weaver enters the battlefield, tap target creature an opponent controls. That creature doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", "When Whirler Rogue enters the battlefield, create two 1/1 colorless Thopter artifact creature tokens with flying.\\nTap two untapped artifacts you control: Target creature can't be blocked this turn.", 'When Wicked Guardian enters the battlefield, you may have it deal 2 damage to another creature you control. If you do, draw a card.', "When Wicked Wolf enters the battlefield, it fights up to one target creature you don't control.\\nSacrifice a Food: Put a +1/+1 counter on Wicked Wolf. It gains indestructible until end of turn. Tap it.", "When a creature enters the battlefield, sacrifice Monkey Cage and create X 2/2 green Monkey creature tokens, where X is that creature's mana value.", 'Whenever Angelic Cub becomes the target of a spell or ability for the first time each turn, put a +1/+1 counter on it.\\nAs long as Angelic Cub has three or more +1/+1 counters on it, it has flying.', 'Whenever Ashcoat of the Shadow Swarm attacks or blocks, other Rats you control get +X/+X until end of turn, where X is the number of Rats you control.\\nAt the beginning of your end step, you may mill four cards. If you do, return up to two Rat creature cards from your graveyard to your hand. (To mill a card, put the top card of your library into your graveyard.)', 'Whenever Blood Artist or another creature dies, target player loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever Borderland Marauder attacks, it gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Brazen Wolves attacks, it gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Coalhauler Swine is dealt damage, it deals that much damage to each player.', "Whenever Engulfing Slagwurm blocks or becomes blocked by a creature, destroy that creature. You gain life equal to that creature's toughness.", 'Whenever Fallowsage becomes tapped, you may draw a card.', "Whenever Frenzied Goblin attacks, you may pay {R}. If you do, target creature can't block this turn.", 'Whenever Goblin Psychopath attacks or blocks, flip a coin. If you lose the flip, the next time it would deal combat damage this turn, it deals that damage to you instead.', 'Whenever Grotag Night-Runner deals combat damage to a player, exile the top card of your library. You may play that card this turn.', 'Whenever Imperial Recovery Unit attacks, return target creature or Vehicle card with mana value 2 or less from your graveyard to your hand.\\nCrew 2 (Tap any number of creatures you control with total power 2 or more: This Vehicle becomes an artifact creature until end of turn.)', "Whenever Kessig Cagebreakers attacks, create a 2/2 green Wolf creature token that's tapped and attacking for each creature card in your graveyard.", 'Whenever Leonin Warleader attacks, create two 1/1 white Cat creature tokens with lifelink that are tapped and attacking.', 'Whenever Library Larcenist attacks, draw a card.', "Whenever Marit Lage's Slumber or another snow permanent enters the battlefield under your control, scry 1.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if you control ten or more snow permanents, sacrifice Marit Lage's Slumber. If you do, create Marit Lage, a legendary 20/20 black Avatar creature token with flying and indestructible.", 'Whenever Order of the Golden Cricket attacks, you may pay {W}. If you do, it gains flying until end of turn.', "Whenever Raiders' Karve attacks, look at the top card of your library. If it's a land card, you may put it onto the battlefield tapped.\\nCrew 3 (Tap any number of creatures you control with total power 3 or more: This Vehicle becomes an artifact creature until end of turn.)", 'Whenever Sage of the Falls or another non-Human creature enters the battlefield under your control, you may draw a card. If you do, discard a card.', 'Whenever Saltwater Stalwart deals damage to an opponent, target player draws a card.', "Whenever Takenuma Bleeder attacks or blocks, you lose 1 life if you don't control a Demon.", 'Whenever Task Force becomes the target of a spell or ability, it gets +0/+3 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Undead Augur or another Zombie you control dies, you draw a card and you lose 1 life.', "Whenever a Dragon enters the battlefield under your control, put a gold counter on Dragon's Hoard.\\n{T}, Remove a gold counter from Dragon's Hoard: Draw a card.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.", 'Whenever a Merfolk you control deals combat damage to a player, draw a card.', 'Whenever a Swamp enters the battlefield under your control, choose one —\\n• You draw a card and you lose 1 life.\\n• Dread Presence deals 2 damage to any target and you gain 2 life.', 'Whenever a Vehicle you control attacks, choose one —\\n• That Vehicle gains first strike until end of turn.\\n• Untap Kitsune Ace.', 'Whenever a creature dealt damage by Dread Slaver this turn dies, return it to the battlefield under your control. That creature is a black Zombie in addition to its other colors and types.', 'Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Whenever a permanent you control becomes untapped, Wake Thrasher gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Whenever a source an opponent controls deals damage to you, that player sacrifices a permanent.', 'Whenever a source deals damage to Nested Ghoul, create a 2/2 black Phyrexian Zombie creature token.', "Whenever a source you control deals noncombat damage to an opponent, Chandra's Pyreling gets +1/+0 and gains double strike until end of turn. (It deals both first-strike and regular combat damage.)", 'Whenever a source you control other than Talon of Pain deals damage to an opponent, put a charge counter on Talon of Pain.\\n{X}, {T}, Remove X charge counters from Talon of Pain: It deals X damage to any target.', 'Whenever an artifact enters the battlefield under your control, Reckless Fireweaver deals 1 damage to each opponent.', 'Whenever an artifact enters the battlefield under your control, Weldfast Wingsmith gains flying until end of turn.', 'Whenever an attacking creature you control dies, Brazen Cannonade deals 2 damage to each opponent.\\nRaid — At the beginning of your postcombat main phase, if you attacked with a creature this turn, exile the top card of your library. Until end of combat on your next turn, you may play that card.', 'Whenever an opponent casts a spell, you may draw a card unless that player pays {1}.', 'Whenever an opponent draws a card, Ob Nixilis, the Hate-Twisted deals 1 damage to that player.\\n[−2]: Destroy target creature. Its controller draws two cards.', 'Whenever an opponent is dealt noncombat damage, creatures you control get +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Whenever another Goblin you control becomes blocked, sacrifice it. If you do, it deals 4 damage to each creature blocking it.\\nSacrifice two Mountains: Create two 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens.', 'Whenever another creature dies, or a creature card is put into a graveyard from anywhere other than the battlefield, or a creature card leaves your graveyard, Syr Konrad, the Grim deals 1 damage to each opponent.\\n{1}{B}: Each player mills a card. (They each put the top card of their library into their graveyard.)', 'Whenever another creature enters the battlefield under your control, creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', "Whenever another creature enters the battlefield under your control, you gain 1 life.\\n{4}{W}, {T}: Exile another target creature you control, then return it to the battlefield under its owner's control.", 'Whenever another creature enters the battlefield, untap Midnight Guard.', 'Whenever another creature you control attacks, it gets +0/+1 until end of turn.', 'Whenever another creature you control dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Gavony Unhallowed.', 'Whenever another creature you control leaves the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on Ninth Bridge Patrol.', 'Whenever another green creature enters the battlefield under your control, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.', 'Whenever another nontoken creature dies, you may create a 1/1 black Rat creature token.\\nRats you control have deathtouch.', "Whenever another nontoken creature enters the battlefield under your control, if it wasn't cast, create a token that's a copy of that creature, except it's a 0/1 white Illusion.\\n{1}{W}, Sacrifice five Illusions: Exile target nonland permanent.", 'Whenever equipped creature attacks, Heart-Piercer Bow deals 1 damage to target creature defending player controls.\\nEquip {1} ({1}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', "Whenever equipped creature attacks, look at the top card of your library. If it's a land card, you may put it onto the battlefield tapped.\\nEquip {1} ({1}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)", 'Whenever equipped creature becomes blocked by a creature, you may draw two cards.\\nEquip {1}', 'Whenever one or more other Elves enter the battlefield under your control, create a 1/1 green Elf Warrior creature token. This ability triggers only once each turn.\\n{5}{G}{G}: Elves you control get +2/+2 and gain deathtouch until end of turn.', 'Whenever one or more tokens enter the battlefield under your control, put that many +1/+1 counters on Woodland Champion.', 'Whenever you attack with two or more creatures, draw a card.', 'Whenever you cast a creature spell with mana value 5 or greater, that creature enters the battlefield with X additional +1/+1 counters on it, where X is its mana value minus 4.\\nCreatures you control with three or more +1/+1 counters on them have haste.\\n{T}: Add {G}.', 'Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, put a +1/+1 counter on Spellgorger Weird.', 'Whenever you cast an Elf spell, you may create a 1/1 green Elf Warrior creature token.', 'Whenever you cast an enchantment spell, create a 4/4 white Angel creature token with flying.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, create a 1/1 red Elemental creature token.', "Whenever you cast your first spell during each opponent's turn, draw a card.", "Whenever you cast your first spell during each opponent's turn, you may tap or untap target nonland permanent.", 'Whenever you cycle a card, you may have Reptilian Reflection become a 5/4 Dinosaur creature with trample and haste in addition to its other types until end of turn.', 'Whenever you cycle another card, Drannith Stinger deals 1 damage to each opponent.\\nCycling {1} ({1}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', "Whenever you discard a card, exile that card from your graveyard.\\n{2}, {T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.\\n{4}, {T}, Sacrifice Bag of Holding: Return all cards exiled with Bag of Holding to their owner's hand.", 'Whenever you draw a card, you may pay {1}. When you do, you may tap or untap target creature.', 'Whenever you draw your second card each turn, Bloodhaze Wolverine gets +1/+1 and gains first strike until end of turn.', 'Whenever you draw your second card each turn, Irencrag Pyromancer deals 3 damage to any target.', 'Whenever you draw your second card each turn, Mystic Skyfish gains flying until end of turn.', 'Whenever you draw your second card each turn, create a 2/2 blue Drake creature token with flying.\\nWhenever you draw your fifth card each turn, Alandra, Sky Dreamer and Drakes you control each get +X/+X until end of turn, where X is the number of cards in your hand.', 'Whenever you draw your second card each turn, create two 1/1 black Rat creature tokens.', "Whenever you draw your second card each turn, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature you control.\\n[+1]: Draw a card.\\n[−7]: Creatures you control can't be blocked this turn.", 'Whenever you gain life for the first time each turn, create a 1/1 white Cat creature token.\\n{2}{W}: Another target Cleric gains lifelink until end of turn.', 'Whenever you gain life, Kalastria Nightwatch gains flying until end of turn.', 'Whenever you gain life, Nirkana Assassin gains deathtouch until end of turn. (Any amount of damage it deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)', 'Whenever you gain life, each opponent loses 1 life.', "Whenever you gain life, put a +1/+1 counter on Ajani's Pridemate.", 'Whenever you gain life, put a +1/+1 counter on Bloodbond Vampire.', 'Whenever you gain life, target opponent loses that much life.\\n{3}{B}{B}: Creatures you control gain lifelink until end of turn.', 'Whenever you gain life, you may pay {2}. If you do, draw a card.\\n{3}{W}: Create a 1/1 white Soldier creature token with lifelink.', 'Whenever you gain life, you may pay {W}. If you do, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.', "Whenever you sacrifice a permanent, put a +1/+1 counter on Blood Aspirant.\\n{1}{R}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature or enchantment: Blood Aspirant deals 1 damage to target creature. That creature can't block this turn.", 'You draw three cards and you lose 3 life.', "You may cast Harbinger of the Tides as though it had flash if you pay {2} more to cast it. (You may cast it any time you could cast an instant.)\\nWhen Harbinger of the Tides enters the battlefield, you may return target tapped creature an opponent controls to its owner's hand.", 'You may have Gigantoplasm enter the battlefield as a copy of any creature on the battlefield, except it has "{X}: This creature has base power and toughness X/X."', 'You may have Mirror Image enter the battlefield as a copy of a creature you control.', 'You may have Pirated Copy enter the battlefield as a copy of any creature on the battlefield, except it\'s a Pirate in addition to its other types and it has "Whenever this creature or another creature with the same name deals combat damage to a player, you draw a card."', 'You may look at the top card of your library any time.\\nYou may play snow lands and cast snow spells from the top of your library.\\nWhenever another snow permanent enters the battlefield under your control, you may pay {G}, {W}, or {U}. If you do, put a +1/+1 counter on Isu the Abominable.', "You may pay {1}{W} and exile a creature card from your graveyard rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nFlying", "You may play lands and cast Insect spells from your graveyard.\\nWhenever another Insect you control dies, put it on the bottom of its owner's library, then mill two cards. (Put the top two cards of your library into your graveyard.)\\n{1}{B/G}: Target Insect gets +1/+0 and gains deathtouch until end of turn. ({B/G} can be paid with either {B} or {G}.)", "Zombies you control get +1/+1.\\nWhen Liliana's Mastery enters the battlefield, create two 2/2 black Zombie creature tokens.", "Zombies you control have menace. (They can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)\\n{3}{B}, Exile a creature card from your graveyard: Create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.", "[+1]: Chandra, Flame's Fury deals 2 damage to any target.\\n[−2]: Chandra, Flame's Fury deals 4 damage to target creature and 2 damage to that creature's controller.\\n[−8]: Chandra, Flame's Fury deals 10 damage to target player and each creature that player controls.", '[+1]: Create a 1/1 colorless Thopter artifact creature token with flying.\\n[0]: Draw a card. If you control three or more artifacts, draw two cards instead.\\n[−9]: You get an emblem with "At the beginning of your end step, search your library for a permanent card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle."', '[+1]: Create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token. Mill two cards.\\n[−3]: Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield. That creature is a black Zombie in addition to its other colors and types.\\n[−7]: Destroy all non-Zombie creatures.', "[+1]: Put a loyalty counter on Gideon, Champion of Justice for each creature target opponent controls.\\n[0]: Until end of turn, Gideon, Champion of Justice becomes a Human Soldier creature with power and toughness each equal to the number of loyalty counters on him and gains indestructible. He's still a planeswalker. Prevent all damage that would be dealt to him this turn.\\n[−15]: Exile all other permanents.", '[+1]: Tap target permanent. It doesn\'t untap during its controller\'s next untap step.\\n[−2]: Draw a card for each tapped creature target player controls.\\n[−8]: You get an emblem with "You have no maximum hand size" and "Whenever a card is put into your graveyard from anywhere, you may return it to your hand."', '[+1]: Until end of turn, Sarkhan, the Dragonspeaker becomes a legendary 4/4 red Dragon creature with flying, indestructible, and haste. (He doesn\'t lose loyalty while he\'s not a planeswalker.)\\n[−3]: Sarkhan, the Dragonspeaker deals 4 damage to target creature.\\n[−6]: You get an emblem with "At the beginning of your draw step, draw two additional cards" and "At the beginning of your end step, discard your hand."', '[+1]: You gain life equal to the number of creatures you control plus the number of planeswalkers you control.\\n[−2]: Create a 2/2 white Cat Soldier creature token named Ajani\'s Pridemate with "Whenever you gain life, put a +1/+1 counter on Ajani\'s Pridemate."\\n[0]: If you have at least 15 life more than your starting life total, exile Ajani, Strength of the Pride and each artifact and creature your opponents control.', '[+4]: Target player exiles a card from their hand.\\n[−3]: Exile target permanent.\\n[−14]: Restart the game, leaving in exile all non-Aura permanent cards exiled with Karn Liberated. Then put those cards onto the battlefield under your control.', '{1}, Sacrifice Thrashing Brontodon: Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', '{1}, {T}, Exile a creature card from your graveyard: Create a Treasure token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Add one mana of any color.")', '{1}, {T}: Blisterspit Gremlin deals 1 damage to each opponent.\\nWhenever you cast a noncreature spell, untap Blisterspit Gremlin.', "{1}, {T}: Pyre-Sledge Arsonist deals X damage to any target, where X is the number of permanents you've sacrificed this turn.", '{1}, {T}: Tap target creature with mana value 2 or greater.', "{1}, {T}: Target creature can't attack this turn. Put a brick counter on Edifice of Authority.\\n{1}, {T}: Until your next turn, target creature can't attack or block and its activated abilities can't be activated. Activate only if there are three or more brick counters on Edifice of Authority.", '{1}{B}, Discard a creature card: Draw a card. If the discarded card was a Zombie card, create a tapped 2/2 black Zombie creature token.', '{1}{B}, Pay 2 life: Return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', '{1}{B}, Sacrifice a creature: Target player loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.', '{1}{B}, Sacrifice a creature: You gain 1 life and draw a card.', '{1}{B}, {T}, Exile a creature card from your graveyard: Target opponent loses 3 life.', '{1}{B}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: You gain 1 life and draw a card.', '{1}{B}: Return Reassembling Skeleton from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped.', '{1}{G}, Sacrifice Caustic Caterpillar: Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', '{1}{R}, Sacrifice a Goblin: Arms Dealer deals 4 damage to target creature.', '{1}{R}: Weaselback Redcap gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', "{1}{S}: Frostpeak Yeti can't be blocked this turn. ({S} can be paid with one mana from a snow source.)", '{1}{U}, {T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.', '{1}{U}, {T}: You may tap or untap target creature.', '{1}{W}: Another target Vehicle you control becomes an artifact creature until end of turn.\\nCrew 4 (Tap any number of creatures you control with total power 4 or more: This Vehicle becomes an artifact creature until end of turn.)', '{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Expedition Map: Search your library for a land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', '{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Vial of Dragonfire: It deals 2 damage to target creature.', '{2}: Target artifact creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.\\n{2}: Target artifact creature gains your choice of flying, trample, or haste until end of turn.', "{2}: Target snow land you control becomes a 4/4 Elemental creature with hexproof and haste until end of turn. It's still a land. (A creature with hexproof can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)", '{2}{G}, {T}, Sacrifice Oashra Cultivator: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{2}{G}: Pestilent Wolf gains deathtouch until end of turn.', "{2}{G}: Target creature you control can't be blocked by creatures with power 2 or less this turn.", '{2}{G}: Wily Bandar gains indestructible until end of turn. (Damage and effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy it.)', '{2}{R}: Coalborn Entity deals 1 damage to target creature token, player, or planeswalker.', '{2}{R}: Lavastep Raider gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', '{3}, Sacrifice a creature or planeswalker: You gain 1 life and draw a card.', '{3}, {T}: Investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")', '{3}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.', "{3}, {T}: Target player puts the bottom card of their library into their graveyard. If it's a creature card, you create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.", "{3}: Exile another target creature you control, then return it to the battlefield under its owner's control.\\nWhenever another creature enters the battlefield under your control, you may pay {G/W}. If you do, put a +1/+1 counter on it. If it's a Unicorn, put two +1/+1 counters on it instead. ({G/W} can be paid with either {G} or {W}.)", "{3}{B}{B}: Monstrosity 3. (If this creature isn't monstrous, put three +1/+1 counters on it and it becomes monstrous.)\\nAs long as Sinuous Vermin is monstrous, it has menace. (It can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)", '{3}{G}: Mild-Mannered Librarian becomes a Werewolf. Put two +1/+1 counters on it and you draw a card. Activate only once.', '{3}{W}: Put a +1/+1 counter on another target attacking creature you control. If that creature is a Cat, it gains first strike until end of turn.', '{4}, {T}: Create a 1/1 colorless Thopter artifact creature token with flying.', '{4}: Locthwain Gargoyle gets +2/+0 and gains flying until end of turn.', '{4}{B}: Return Durable Coilbug from your graveyard to your hand.', '{4}{B}{B}, Exile Suspicious Shambler from your graveyard: Create two 2/2 black Zombie creature tokens. Activate only as a sorcery.', "{4}{G}: Double Reckless Amplimancer's power and toughness until end of turn.", "{4}{S}{S}: Monstrosity 2. (If this creature isn't monstrous, put two +1/+1 counters on it and it becomes monstrous. {S} can be paid with one mana from a snow source.)\\nAs long as Chillerpillar is monstrous, it has flying.", '{5}{G}: Creatures you control get +1/+1 and gain trample until end of turn.', '{5}{G}: Kraul Warrior gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', '{7}, {T}, Sacrifice Universal Solvent: Destroy target permanent.', "{7}: Create a token that's a copy of target artifact. That token gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step.", '{B}, Sacrifice a creature: Target player discards a card. Activate only as a sorcery.', '{B}, {T}, Discard a card: Each player loses 2 life.', '{B}, {T}, Pay 1 life: Put a +1/+1 counter on Cruel Sadist.\\n{2}{B}, {T}, Remove X +1/+1 counters from Cruel Sadist: It deals X damage to target creature.', '{G}, Sacrifice Giant Caterpillar: Create a 1/1 green Insect creature token with flying named Butterfly at the beginning of the next end step.', '{S}, {T}: Tap target artifact or creature. ({S} can be paid with one mana from a snow source.)', '{T}, Discard a card: Draw a card.', '{T}, Sacrifice Evolving Wilds: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', "{T}, Sacrifice Liliana's Steward: Target opponent discards a card. Activate only as a sorcery.", '{T}, Sacrifice Phyrexian Plaguelord: Target creature gets -4/-4 until end of turn.\\nSacrifice a creature: Target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.', '{T}, Sacrifice an artifact: Barrage Ogre deals 2 damage to any target.', '{T}, Sacrifice another creature: Each opponent loses 2 life and you gain 2 life.', '{T}: Add one mana of any color. If you control a creature with power 4 or greater, add two mana of any one color instead.', '{T}: Add one mana of any type that a land you control could produce.', '{T}: Add two mana of any one color. Spend this mana only to cast artifact spells or activate abilities of artifacts.', '{T}: Add {B}.\\n{1}{B}{B}, {T}, Sacrifice Infernal Idol: You draw two cards and you lose 2 life.', '{T}: Add {C}.', "{T}: Add {C}. If you control an Urza's Mine and an Urza's Power-Plant, add {C}{C}{C} instead.", "{T}: Add {C}. If you control an Urza's Mine and an Urza's Tower, add {C}{C} instead.", "{T}: Add {C}. If you control an Urza's Power-Plant and an Urza's Tower, add {C}{C} instead.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\nBasic landcycling {1} ({1}, Discard this card: Search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}: Mishra's Factory becomes a 2/2 Assembly-Worker artifact creature until end of turn. It's still a land.\\n{T}: Target Assembly-Worker creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Warped Landscape: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}, {T}: Draw a card. Activate only if you control a creature with power 4 or greater.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{4}, {T}: Investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{4}{B}, {T}, Sacrifice Blighted Fen: Target opponent sacrifices a creature.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{7}, {T}: Create a 2/2 colorless Assembly-Worker artifact creature token.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}. Spend this mana only to cast artifact spells or activate abilities of artifacts.\\n{U}, {T}: Search your library for a card named Heart-Piercer Bow or Vial of Dragonfire, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Hedron Archive: Draw two cards.', '{T}: Add {U}.', "{T}: Chandra's Magmutt deals 1 damage to target player or planeswalker.", '{T}: Create X 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens, where X is the number of Goblins you control.', '{T}: Each player creates a colorless artifact token named Banana with "{T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Add {R} or {G}. You gain 2 life."\\nWhenever an artifact an opponent controls is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control that\'s an Ape or a Monkey.\\nWhenever Kibo attacks, defending player sacrifices an artifact.', '{T}: Fireslinger deals 1 damage to any target and 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Goblin Artillery deals 2 damage to any target and 3 damage to you.', '{T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on each artifact creature you control.', '{T}: Put a bounty counter on target creature or planeswalker. Activate only as a sorcery.\\nWhenever a creature or planeswalker an opponent controls with a bounty counter on it is dealt damage, destroy it.', "{T}: Return Wizard Mentor and target creature you control to their owner's hand.", '{T}: Target Assembly-Worker creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{T}: Target attacking creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{T}: Target creature gains haste until end of turn.', "{U}, Sacrifice Aether Spellbomb: Return target creature to its owner's hand.\\n{1}, Sacrifice Aether Spellbomb: Draw a card.", '{W}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature with a +1/+1 counter on it.\\n{4}{W}{W}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.', '{W}, {T}: Tap target creature.', '{X}: Crypt Rats deals X damage to each creature and each player. Spend only black mana on X.', "{X}{G}{G}{G}: Monstrosity X. (If this creature isn't monstrous, put X +1/+1 counters on it and it becomes monstrous.)\\nAs long as Domesticated Hydra is monstrous, it has trample."]
flavor: ['"\'Rat-infested\' sounds so negative. I prefer \'rat-friendly.\'"', '". . . that\'s when I reeled in a human about yay big."', '"A crafter must imbue her weapon with part of her soul—something the Phyrexians are incapable of doing."\\n—Melira', '"A few drops of this, and the trickiest problems simply melt away."\\n—Thamaz, Weldfast inventor', '"Ah, we have a critic."\\n—Orthion, Lavabrink captain', '"Airships are too confining. If I\'m in the sky, I want to feel the wind in my hair and taste the aether."', '"All tinkerers have their heads in the clouds. I don\'t intend to stop there."', '"And Muzzio says my arguments have no teeth."\\n—Selvala, ranger of the Lowlands', '"Angels and inquisitors terrorize villages, but no one seems to notice the stirring out at sea."', '"As long as its roots still reach the soil, I can heal it."', '"As the sun rose behind the Bone Spire, an angel appeared over the charnel fields, bringing a surge of new hope."\\n—Krinnea, *Siege of the Bone Spire*', '"As the traitor hurried across the courtyard, its eyes snapped open. It was time to pay the queen a visit."\\n—*Beyond the Great Henge*', '"Avacyn has deserted you. I welcome your devotion in her stead."', '"Be like the sea: flow around that which is unmovable; for everything else, crash into it unrelentingly."', '"Before Yovus was cut down at Pranticle Peak, she performed which maneuver? Anyone? From the reading?"', '"Bow before the power of *science*!"', '"Build a moat. If we\'re lucky, it can\'t swim."\\n—Syr Branigan, knight of Ardenvale', '"Careful. Leave it running for too long and it\'ll turn the whole building into angels."\\n—Tawnos', '"Come. Bring your brothers. Tonight, you feast on living flesh."\\n—Jadar, ghoulcaller of Nephalia', '"Could you please spare some of your blood for my precious little tree?"', '"Count yourself lucky it only broke your kitesail. Get that close to the nest again and it\'ll be your face."\\n—Huatli', '"Dawn-kissed, he nourishes the golden grain."\\n—Psemilla, Meletian poet', '"Do I really look like that? I\'m . . . beautiful!"', '"Do try to pull your weight, Geralf. I feel like I\'m doing everything."\\n—Ghoulcaller Gisa', '"Don\'t worry, folks. We\'re perfectly safe here. That\'s a banana processing plant."', '"Don\'t worry, sweet brother. Help is on the way."\\n—Ghoulcaller Gisa', '"Duty and law are the foundation on which civilization stands. They must not fall, for when they do, they take everything with them."\\n—Lord Konda', '"Each night, the artificer tucked the little doll into a locked drawer. Each morning, she awoke to find it waiting beside her with some new bauble."\\n—"The Artificer\'s Apprentice"', '"Even after death, a wealth of serviceable biomass remains."\\n—Phyrexian progress notes', '"Even rats hoard their treasures. Are your precious things so different?"\\n—Izoni', '"Even your shadow is too foul to tolerate."', '"Ever onward, ever skyward."', '"Every death has a web of consequences. Our job is to find the spider."', '"Every footfall on the forest floor is a heartbeat sending strength into my veins."', '"Every scratch tells a story, and every notch has a name. Four generations have held this blade. You shall not disappoint them."\\n—Initiation of Laena, skyhunter', '"Every seed holds strength and teaches patience."', '"Everybody but me—CHARGE!"', '"Fear of fire is a sensible instinct. If I were you, I\'d be terrified."', '"Fear the dark if you must, but don\'t mistake sunlight for safety."\\n—Josu Vess', '"Feast, for your next meal may be your last!"', '"Fill the sky with stuff!"', '"Fire is always dancing, leaping and whirling, seeking more fuel. It never rests, so why should I?"\\n—Chandra Nalaar', '"Flee all you like. The further you run the more firmly I feel your heartbeat."', '"Fleshy, with just a hint of leather. A fine vintage."', '"Forward! Until the horizon is ours!"\\n—Khemses, charioteer', '"From a great bonfire at the dawn of time, the first Gruul kindled their rage. The same flame burns in you."\\n—Kroshkar, Gruul shaman', '"Gather round and tell me all from the courts and castles."', '"Gazing at the unicorn, I felt closer to the majesty of Nyx than I ever had before."\\n—Oineus, traveling merchant', '"Ghoulcallers trying to get in, geists trying to get out . . . . This duty is never dull."', '"Give me eight walkers, I\'ll give you the city."\\n—Dovin Baan', '"Gold without freedom might as well be lead."\\n—Angrath', '"Guaranteed to leave your enemies sufficiently stabbed, bitten, cleaved, or exploded."\\n—Grezkrick\'s Emporium motto', '"He displays a perverse charisma fueled by avarice. Highly dangerous. Recommend civil sanctions."\\n—Agmand Sarv, Azorius hussar', '"Here lies Gond, hero of Safehold Taldwen. May he ever guide our quest."', '"How many claws does a monster have? Exactly one more than you\'ve accounted for."\\n—Alux, Skysail defender', '"How strong is he? Well, I once lost control of the plow, and he carved a furrow right through my house! Didn\'t even slow down."\\n—Guldir, Beskir farmer', '"I always attack from where their spyglasses can\'t see."', '"I am a dragonslayer for Lord Silumgar. There is no dragon save him whom I fear."\\n—Xathi the Infallible', '"I am the rock of the polis. Death only strengthens me."', '"I appreciate things that exceed expectations."\\n—Mizzix', '"I can bring down anything in Zagoth, but for some quarry the ratio of fight to meat is too high."\\n—Master Hunter Chevill', '"I can give you strength, but you\'ll have to bring your own courage."', '"I can no longer stand by as these Skirsdag infiltrators rot the church from within. Even the Lunarch Council is compromised. What a fool I\'ve been."\\n—Odric', '"I can\'t bear to see another plane broken before I make my own home whole. I\'m sorry, but my watch is over."', '"I can\'t bear to watch these things put themselves back together, Geralf. They remind me of the time you tried to cut your own hair: a tragic abomination!"\\n—Ghoulcaller Gisa', '"I do not fear death. I know my soul will rise to Starnheim, where I will feast forever among valkyries and heroes. Can you say the same?"', '"I don\'t think they\'ll appreciate my . . . adjustments."\\n—Karavin, renegade saboteur', '"I don\'t understand. He\'s normally so well behaved!"', '"I hope you took notes before it exploded."', '"I know they\'re unstoppable fighters created to harvest souls—it\'s just they\'re so rude about it."\\n—Kaya', '"I like to think Kytheon keeps watch over all of us."', '"I often think on how excited they must feel to be chosen as my prey."', '"I prefer to weave my magic through oni blood, but yours will do in a pinch."', '"I saw the devastation when the juggernauts crashed the walls of An Karras. Then I got to thinking."\\n—Janji, sylvan druid', '"I specialize in missing manuscripts, pilfered poetry, and lifted letters."', '"I think Chandra just wanted something to blame random scorch marks on."\\n—Jace Beleren', '"I told you this one would be a handful."', '"I trained with the Ghitu, and I respect the fire as they do."', '"I use maps to find out where explorers have already been. Then I go the other way."\\n—Javad Nasrin, Ondu relic hunter', '"I was not convinced you had a soul until I saw it for myself."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"I was wrong. Zendikar isn\'t after me. It isn\'t after any of us. It\'s not evil or vengeful. It\'s magnificent . . . but it\'s in pain."\\n—Nissa Revane', '"I will be your most demanding master, Liliana. But I have great things in mind for you."', '"I will protect the less fortunate. I will love bravely. I will face despair and fight on. As a Capashen, I can do no less."', '"I would rather cast myself into the abyss than let my blood stain the cap of those monsters."\\n—Syr Alin, the Lion\'s Claw', '"I would welcome her into my pack with honor."\\n—Arlinn Kord', '"I\'ll take it from here, soldier."', '"I\'ll teach you the leyline paratrigonometrics, no problem. But you need to show me how to make that fiery swirly thing."\\n—Zimone, to Rootha', '"I\'m about to make you famous. From the golden city to High and Dry, they\'ll talk about how fast you died!"', '"I\'m feeling generous. I\'ll let you choose the blade that slays you."', '"I\'ve been carrying a sword since before you were born. I wouldn\'t give up my oath for all the peace and comfort in the world."', '"I\'ve forgotten more spells than you will ever know."', '"I\'ve lit most everything on fire—trees, rocks, even the water. Now it\'s time to burn the clouds."', '"I\'ve seen them survive lava, trampling, and a moloch\'s digestive system. They just roll out and get on with their lives!"\\n—Gannet, Skysail zoologist', '"If I\'m going, I\'m taking you with me!"', '"If a careless elf ends up caught in a spider\'s web, we must expect nature to take its course. Do not blame the spider for being a spider."\\n—Dellin Berting, Tolarian entomologist', '"If a vampire were feeding on you every night, wouldn\'t you have bite marks? Stop wasting my time."\\n—Donya, village healer', '"If it were merely lethal, that would be sufficient. The art, however, is in maximizing the suffering it causes."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"If that brain can\'t figure out the secret of the serum, then add more brains."\\n—Rhmir, Hand of the Augur', '"If we didn\'t guard our secrets, they wouldn\'t remain secrets for long."\\n—Gadwick, the Wizened', '"If you hear a groaning noise in the cellar, don\'t investigate. Don\'t split up. Just lock the door and barricade it."\\n—Emili, guard captain', '"If you think yourself a chief, then prove your might."\\n—Gar-Tun, Mistvalley silverback', '"If you would taste the wisdom of the oni, be prepared to salt it with your blood."\\n—Kiku, Night\'s Flower', '"If you\'re going to run for cover, you should start now."', '"If you\'ve been at this as long as I have, nothing can surprise you. That\'s the hope, at least."', '"If your mech is factory standard, you might as well be walking."', '"In memories, we can find our deepest reserves of strength."', '"In you go, big guy. Watch your head."', '"Innistrad\'s ghoulcallers are talented enough, but let me show you what someone with real power can create."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"Is it purebred? No, but it\'s pure fire."\\n—Chandra Nalaar', '"Is there anything in Guul Draz that *doesn\'t* suck the life out of you?"\\n—Tarsa, Sea Gate sell-sword', '"It is not just our people I try to rescue. It is our culture, and our hope that we can return to greatness."', '"It was difficult to tell whether the piles of gore within their warrens were mere trash heaps, sacred altars, or warnings."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. IV*', '"It was right here a second ago . . ."', '"It\'s contemplative, resourceful, and original. Everything else aside, it\'s the perfect student."\\n—Naban, dean of iteration', '"It\'s either terrified or extremely mad at us, definitely one of the two."\\n—Jonald, mission naturalist', '"It\'s odd to see the apes rip down trees to arm themselves in defense of their forests."\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, elvish hunter', '"Just a collage of images: cryptoliths, the sea, a tangle of shipwrecks."', '"Kalitas may have returned to mindless servitude beneath the Eldrazi, but we say never again."\\n—Drana, Kalastria bloodchief', '"Lady Wren is the one merchant in Keyhole Downs who isn\'t running a scam."\\n—Mirela, Azorius hussar', '"Leave no scraps, lest you attract pests."\\n—Mardu threat', '"Let me give you a hand. He won\'t be needing it; he\'s left-handed. Also dead."', '"Let the forest spread! From salt, stone, and fen, let the new trees rise."\\n—Molimo, maro-sorcerer', '"Let the vampires join us. In this war, we no longer have the luxury of choosing our comrades."\\n—General Tazri, allied commander', '"Light a torch and deliver this letter" were his instructions, which he unfortunately reversed.', '"Like fruits in the field, we will be harvested when the season is right."', '"Linear growth? What am I, a first-year?"', '"Looks like I need a new test subject. Any volunteers?"', '"Madness can\'t touch a mind ignited by genius."', '"May the light shine through me to guide the lost."', '"Mere death brings no pleasure. Pleasure comes from watching fools scratch and claw to save their wretched lives from the inevitable."\\n—Ob Nixilis', '"My cats have taught me more about the sacred than anything in some old ruin."', '"My family sheltered in her light, the dark was content to wait."\\n—Crovax', '"Nature is not always gentle or kind, but all life begets life."\\n—Marwyn of Llanowar', '"Neither time nor death could keep me from upholding our pact."', '"No! It\'s all wrong! I need more. Bring me more!"', '"Not again."\\n—Hans', '"Now is not the time for your light to fade."', '"Now that I\'ve dealt with your little toys, I can focus on the real problem: you."\\n—Chandra Nalaar, to Dovin Baan', '"Oh, Valki. I\'m disappointed in you. How could the god of lies be so gullible?"\\n—Tibalt', '"Oh, sorry—were we racing?"', '"Okay, maybe the 962nd spear will be the one that gets \'em!"\\n—Kreech, ballista operator', '"Once, vampires ruled this world, commanding the fear and respect that befit our noble blood. Have we truly sunk so low?"\\n—Sorin Markov', '"One alone is fearsome; one among many is unstoppable."\\n—Benalish proverb', '"One faith, but many hands in victory."', '"Only the Ancestor should be revered."\\n—Mystic heretic', '"Only the worthy may pass."', '"Only those who give the dragons the respect they deserve may bear our title."', '"Open grave available, only one previous tenant."\\n—Sign on cemetery gate', '"Our ancestors grew complacent in their divinity, allowing their lessers to topple them. Never again."', '"Our creations are more than mere things. They have life in them, little bits of ourselves."\\n—Saheeli Rai', '"Our duty does not stop at our borders."', '"Pain isn\'t a negative stimulus. Pain is a sign of your imperfection."\\n—Sheoldred, Whispering One', '"Permission to haunt aboard, cap\'n?"', '"Please don\'t feed the beetles."\\n—Promenade warning sign', '"Prepare to be boarded! Or don\'t. I\'m coming over either way."', '"Reality is always much duller and grayer than what your imagination can conjure."', '"Release that which was never caged."\\n—Spellbomb inscription', '"Research is hardly the dry, serious pastime outsiders make it out to be."', '"River and sea, jungle and sky. Water flows freely between the two halves of the world. We are creatures of the water."\\n—Shaper Tuvasa', '"See that no one enters or leaves New Prahv today. And notify me at once of any Planeswalker activity."\\n—Dovin Baan', '"Serves you right for rushing ahead."\\n—Kaliea, Sea Gate trapfinder', '"Shame we\'ll never see what all the fuss was about."', '"She\'s quick and fearless, and she\'s never missed a shot. That almost makes up for all the scorch marks she leaves behind."\\n—Captain Lannery Storm', '"Shoo, you little worm tails—go away! My corpses aren\'t your dinner!"\\n—Ghoulcaller Gisa', '"Should you take it in mind to ride a springjack, remember: there are easier ways to fly, and harder ways to break your skull."\\n—Lann of Cloverdell', '"Sit. Fetch. Devastate."', '"Skyknight gear? Well, I have drake-skin gauntlets, supple and fireproof. Or a ceratok chestplate that\'ll stop a crossbow bolt."', '"Some are born to greatness. You were born to scrub greatness\'s floors."', '"Some hid from the storm. I embraced it and learned its name."', '"Sometimes the hardest choice is between two wonders."\\n—Gadwick, the Wizened', '"Stensia blazes with new heat. Nephalia\'s tides are chaotic. And everywhere, this unnatural frost. The land is sending a warning."\\n—Katilda, Dawnhart Prime', '"Sumptuous, carefully fermented, and served with a silky ocular puree. You simply must try a bite."\\n—Varina, Lich Queen', '"Sure, I\'ve got nine lives, but that doesn\'t mean I\'m keen to waste one now."', '"Swords, to me! We must engage their line to protect our archers and mages. Let no one fail this task!"', '"Take what solace you can in the knowledge that you will not be here to witness Zendikar\'s demise."\\n—Ob Nixilis', '"That was a Consulate spy thopter. Leave the caterpillar to its meal."\\n—Pia Nalaar, renegade inventor', '"The Brazen Coalition is a firecannon pointed at our enemies. Goblins like him are the spark to its powder."\\n—Admiral Beckett Brass', '"The Immortal Sun will bring us true eternal life to replace the everlasting shadow of undeath."', '"The Wojek defend the laws. We defend the people."', '"The answers are here. This is the way through the trial."', '"The artificer assured me that the vial is strong enough to contain the dragon\'s breath. I just need to make sure to throw it far enough."\\n—Kunh Mei, last words', '"The best part of a wedding is the cutting of the cake, followed closely by the cutting of the cake decorator."\\n—Olivia Voldaren', '"The chest cavity is cleared of useless meat. I know just what to do with the space."\\n—Gyed, Vault Priest', '"The courier\'s death was regrettable, but then again, she was warned not to touch it."\\n—Lord Xander', '"The currents are strange today, and the fish are fearful. Something\'s stirring in the depths."\\n—Rathstaf, Kannah fisherman', '"The distraction of your life has ended. Now your service begins."\\n—Kalitas, thrall of Ulamog', '"The essence of a lawful society is swift deterrence."', '"The fires of invention burn in all of us. I fight for the freedom to unleash those flames."\\n—Pia Nalaar', '"The first griffins were made by the gods to capture falling stars; they were given the keenest eyes and the swiftest wings, and sent to keep watch above the clouds."\\n—*The Cosmogony*', '"The first rule of politics can be learned from a lowly hornbeetle: it is wise to cultivate powerful friends."\\n—Pythamon, sage of Meletis', '"The flame paints a bright wheel on the sky, then shifts into a stabbing spark. The enemy falls; the smoke of victory rises."\\n—"Legends of the Firedancer"', '"The lands of the God-Pharaoh are suffused with his breath."', '"The monster was gaining on them. Twice it had found them. There was only one place left to hide."\\n—*Tales of the Fae*', '"The old ways still work, but a little tech support never hurts."', '"The perfect assistant is one that\'s responsive, dextrous, and capable of reaching all the high shelves."\\n—Coruk, Esper artificer', '"The promise of victory fills my heart. There is no room for fear."', '"The realm must never yield to the chaos of the wilds."', '"The ruin of the past is the topsoil of the future."\\n—Sokar, former Nef-crop initiate', '"The second stage of the illness: high fever and severe infectiousness."\\n—Phyrexian progress notes', '"The suffering of others is not my concern."', '"The time of condemnation is at hand. Dusk washes over the world, and I consign you to eternal darkness!"', '"The time of salvation is at hand. Dusk washes over the world, and the Legion will rise immortal!"', '"The true measure of all heroes is not what they achieve, but who they inspire."\\n—*Triumph of Gerrard*', '"The undead are not \'awakened.\' They are evicted when there is no room left in the pit for more bodies."', '"The vampires never had gods. We followed our bloodchiefs. Now they are gone. What is left? Destruction and death, my friends. That is enough."', '"The wolves turned on us and a chill swept over me. The pack had a new leader."\\n—Alena, trapper of Kessig', '"The world is already run by all manner of machines. One day, they\'ll remind us of that fact."\\n—Sargis Haz, artificer', '"The young squire gripped her sword as the clanking stranger emerged. It was no knight that had come to challenge her."\\n—*Beyond the Great Henge*', '"There are dark, ancient arts that fascinate even me."\\n—Sorin Markov', '"There are many kinds of duty, and mine is to see our world grow and endure."', '"There are so many of them. It seems they\'ve just been waiting for someone to serve."', '"There is always more to give."', '"There is as much power in winter\'s chill as in summer\'s warmth."', '"There is no age at which you stop learning."', '"There is nothing stronger than many hearts united for a single cause."\\n—Emmara', '"There is nothing you can do that I cannot simply deny."\\n—Ertai, wizard adept', '"There\'s a smoothness to my magic here that I don\'t find on any other plane."', '"There\'s more where that came from!"', '"There\'s no roar so mighty that it can\'t be silenced."', '"There\'s nowhere in Strixhaven I can\'t find. Where do you need to go?"', '"These sailors on our shores are like the dinosaurs that plunder eggs from nests. They live on the labors of others."\\n—Itzama the Crested', '"They put bars on these noble beasts and then wonder why werewolves target our towns."', '"They say perfection is unattainable, but they said that about flight too."', '"This city could certainly use a bit more divine intervention."\\n—Inspector Jillard', '"This is just my warm-up."', '"This one will need direction. After all, each of its eyes is larger than its brain."\\n—Cyla, Lord of the Aerie', '"This world will not be tamed."', '"Those who have never ridden before the wind do not know the true joy of war."', '"Though their ideals are leagues apart, Urza\'s and Mishra\'s creations have a surprising harmony with one another."\\n—Tocasia, journal entry', '"Thraben\'s pleas fall on deaf ears. Ours do not."', '"Through the blood of the wicked, we shall be redeemed. Let us pray."', '"To die for a cause and continue to serve it is the truest mark of loyalty."', '"To escape Littjara, follow a bird."\\n—Tuskeri folklore', '"To invent is to rebel."\\n—Pia Nalaar', '"To see past the veil of death, cross it."\\n—*The Red Book of Mezdrithalik*', '"To wage war, secure peace within yourself."\\n—Emmara', '"Trees are to be venerated and protected . . . except that one."\\n—Marel, Dawnhart witch', '"Unimaginable riches? I assure you, I have a *vivid* imagination."', '"Unwelcome thoughts crowd my mind. Are they my own madness, or the whispers of another?"\\n—Sarkhan Vol', '"Wanna see a neat trick?"', '"Watch over my father. Tell him I\'m safe, but I won\'t come home until I find out how to bring him back to his senses, and Kamigawa is again at peace."\\n—Michiko, letter to General Takeno', '"Water is in the air, the trees, and the earth. Understand its motion, speak its language, and the subtle currents that flow through all living things will fall under your command."', '"We are bearers of the ancient light, keepers of sun-crowned Heliod\'s blessings. Fight, and the light will protect you!"', '"We came to a place where the skin of Zendikar was peeled back and its bones lay bare to the sky."\\n—Greenweaver Mina', '"We don\'t choose who comes here. We choose how long they stay."', '"We entered the church in search of solace, but it became clear we wouldn\'t find it there."\\n—Grete, Order of Saint Traft', '"We leonin have come to rule the plains by taking to the skies."\\n—Raksha Golden Cub', '"We speak the dragons\' language of flame and rage. They speak our language of fury and honor. Together we shall weave a tale of destruction without equal."', '"We\'ll break their lines. The rest of you, follow!"', '"Well, at least it left us a mouse in exchange. Er . . . ugh . . . make that half a mouse."\\n—Binhald, Beskir veteran', '"Well, this can\'t be a good sign."\\n—Old Rutstein', '"Werewolves are an unholy mix of a predator\'s instinct and a human\'s hatred."\\n—Alena, trapper of Kessig', '"What kind of monstrous grave robber leaves the treasures, but takes the bodies?"\\n—Fjall, Beskir elder', '"What use is a stake or holy symbol in the hands of a coward?"', '"What was once formed by masons, shaped by smiths, or given life by mages, I will return to the embrace of the earth."', '"When all else fails, follow the geist\'s lantern."\\n—Vallon, Thraben inspector', '"When one of us prospers, the pride prospers."\\n—Jazal Goldmane', '"When the land is angry, so are they."\\n—Nissa Revane', '"When you\'re on watch, no noise is harmless and no shadow can be ignored."\\n—Olgard of the Skiltfolk', '"Who am I to break up a family?"\\n—Gisa the Mad', '"Who will miss you, drywalker? A wife? A child? Perhaps they will blame the sea for your fate, and teach future generations to stay far away from it."', '"Why are we following the goblin? Can he even read that map?"\\n—Daphne Vail, *Diremore* first mate', '"Why would someone have built ... wait, never mind. Send it to the front lines!"\\n—Commander Grozdan', '"Within minutes, the strange device was indistinguishable from the other upon my workbench."\\n—Tocasia, journal entry', '"Wow, it\'s even *bigger* than I thought! Awesome!"', '"You are not alone. You never were."', '"You can almost see it calculating—are we a tasty enough treat to risk the jump?"\\n—Samila, Murasa Expeditionary House', '"You don\'t find many old werewolf hunters."\\n—Paulin, trapper of Somberwald', '"You don\'t want to know what happens after I put on the goggles."', '"You have always been a promising student, but your arrogance far outstrips your prowess."', '"You have to admit, Gideon—he has great form."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"You never know what day might be your last."', '"You sign. They die. Simple as that."', '"You\'re in luck. I brought enough to share."\\n—Chandra Nalaar', '"You\'ve begun to understand the hedrons\' true purpose," said Ugin. "The Eldrazi can be imprisoned."\\n"And how did that work out last time?" asked Jace.', '"Your sacrifice has been noted and deemed insufficient."\\n—Qal-Sha, priest of Norn', '"Zendikar will fight until it has bled its last."', "A blisterpod's corpse is a scion's cradle.", 'A circus acrobat in life, she kills with such fluid grace that even her victims are awed by her performance.', 'A full coffin is like a full coffer—both are attractive to thieves.', 'A hunger to soar must be sated.', 'A pit yawned open, a column of oily smoke arose, and a towering form hissed, "I accept this offering."', 'A ray of hope in the darkest night.', 'A single drop turns skin to scale and fist to claw.', 'A strong leader means a growing pack.', 'A unicorn chooses only the most virtuous and noble of knights to be its companion.', 'A weapon best suited for those with good aim and steady hands.', 'A wolf pup is always dangerous, because a wolf pup is never alone.', "Aboard her ship, the *Dragon's Smile*, Kari follows no one's rules but her own.", "All of Zendikar's beings sense the upheaval that accompanies the Eldrazi.", 'All seeds share a common bond, calling to each other across infinity.', 'All the wonders of the natural world in one breathtaking microcosm.', 'All things considered, his first day on patrol could have gone better.', 'All who listen hear their own song, a unique melody played just for them.', 'Among the artisans of Sokenzan City, reusing every scrap of metal is a point of pride.', 'An adventure without a companion is hardly an adventure at all.', 'An avatar he sculpts of instinct and force.', "An explorer's essentials in a wild world.", 'Anyone who thinks merrows have more brains than brawn has never been run over by one.', 'Anything can be a weapon if you swing it hard enough.', "Architects find inspiration in the dragon's beauty of form, while artificers are influenced by the function of its fire.", 'Art is unknown to the vedalken—for them, all creations must serve a purpose.', "As Ravnica's wilds expanded, even advocates for nature had to confront fiercer natural threats.", "As eons passed, the rock wore away, revealing the rich colors at the mountain's heart.", 'As if anyone needed another reason to avoid dark, dank cellars.', "As larvae, they burrow into a host's brain to feed upon it, growing until they're large enough to burst free and seek out larger prey.", 'As the Eldrazi adapted to the jungles of Zendikar, some took on the tactics of more familiar predators.', 'As the blaze raced toward her, Syr Ameril closed her eyes and pictured Castle Ardenvale so her last thoughts would be of home.', 'As the hyperstormic generator crept past redline, a being emerged from the arc.', 'As their supplies of etherium dwindled, mechanists sent gargoyles farther and farther afield in search of salvage.', "As tireless as her mount, a skyhunter's vigil is measured in days.", 'Ask a merfolk even a simple question and the answer is a journey far beyond the known.', 'Atarka goblins meet their demise as readily as their Temur counterparts did, but usually under big, winged shadows.', 'Atarka serving-goblins coat themselves with grease imbued with noxious herbs, hoping to discourage their ravenous masters from adding them to the meal.', "Baby dragons can't figure out humans—if they didn't want to be killed, why were they made of meat and treasure?", "Basri carries on his god's legacy, spreading her teachings throughout the Multiverse.", 'Beauty appears in strange places for those with eyes to see it.', 'Better living through metallurgy.', 'Between stitchers, cultists, and scavengers, corpses are in high demand.', 'Blood is the oldest currency.', 'Bottom feeders sometimes rise to the top.', 'Burning something is easy. Choosing a target can be more difficult.', 'By hammer forged, and by hammer undone.', 'Calix was patient, steadily following Elspeth until their destined confrontation.', 'Call one, call them all.', 'Caught between life and death, between land and sea, between thought and oblivion.', 'Consulate-built automatons have a lifetime warranty.', "Courage alone won't keep you alive.", 'Danger often lurks in the allure of crystal shards.', "Deciding the house's ownership through a wizard duel had sounded like a brilliant idea at the time.", "Denizens of the wilds don't always seek to harm intruders. Sometimes they simply misplace them.", 'Descendant of a vanished land, student of a forgotten general, and master of blades no smith could forge anew. He honors them all by living a life worthy of song.', "Despite the name, they'll happily devour the flesh too.", 'Devils sow chaos and reap panic.', "Don't underestimate the aerodynamic qualities of the common goblin.", 'Dragon birth lairs are littered with treasure to entice the young from their eggs.', 'Duplication is neither thievery nor flattery. It is efficiency.', "Dust and memory are all that remain in Ulamog's wake.", 'Each bronze disk on its harness is an offering from a young Temur hunter, a sign of respect to the spirits of the wild.', "Each cryptolith twists the plane's mana, bending its flow to a singular purpose.", 'Emphatic words with powerful gestures. Clearly this was playtime.', "Entry 434: There's more to Avacyn's madness . . .", 'Eventually, the school would resort to hiring a kraken to guard the more dangerous tomes in the Biblioplex.', "Ever since the disaster, the city's survivors viewed the star-strewn sky with dread.", 'Every attack is a test of your defenses. Every hit marks the map of your defeat.', 'Every footstep is a prayer, every road a temple.', 'Every leaf, tree, and building in Kujar has been placed to achieve maximum harmony, in accordance with the elvish philosophy known as the Great Conduit.', 'Every soldier has a place to stand and a role to play.', 'Every storm has an eye.', 'Everyone who could still lift a weapon had a part in retaking Sea Gate.', "Everything from damaged furniture to inconvenient corpses becomes fuel for Ziatora's ever-burning foundry.", 'Evil is never absent, only hidden.', 'Face of innocence. Hand of death. Designed by Edmund McMillen', 'Fairgoers were delighted to find that even outside the fairgrounds, Ghirapur was a city of wonders.', "Fallen Phyrexians were transmuted into elementals by Gaea long ago, but Yavimaya's other inhabitants still regard them with unease.", 'Far from human eyes, birds flit between vivid blossoms in a hidden paradise.', 'Feed on food, you eventually rot. Feed on rot, you live forever.\\n—Kraul saying', 'Felidars that make it through their first year of life can easily live to see a hundred years more.', 'Finders, keepers.', 'Fire never dies alone.', 'First your whole life flashes before your eyes. Then you have considerable time to reflect on every regret as you plummet.', "Fools believe that Kolaghan's brood follows lightning storms. The wise know that it is the other way around.", 'For Mittens, it was just another day at the beach.', "For Sarkhan Vol, the dragon is the purest expression of life's savage splendor.", 'For a moment they stood tall, all fear forgotten.', 'For most, war is a calamity. For some, an opportunity. And for the very few, a pleasure.', 'For some customers, the old apothecary shop still opens its doors.', 'For the first time in her life, Vraska tried to prevent death.', 'For vampires, blood carries more than life. Memories long eroded from the minds of bloodchiefs can be reclaimed from the veins of their sired kin.', 'Formerly oppressed by the polis of Meletis, leonin occasionally "mistake" their old enemies for game.', 'Freed from their respective labs, the two weirds formed a partnership, feeding on the arcane energies of war.', 'Freshly promoted to "first rock," Zaz was eager to make an impact.', 'From its cocoon, a flurry takes flight.', "From the highest tiers of Dawn's Light Palace to the deepest shade of Wren's Run, the silver notes of the horn shimmer through the air, and all who hear it feel its pull.", 'Gentle hands of stone whisk the careless from the crumbling ruins of Pillardrop.', 'Getting caught was bad enough, but being rolled to the the detention center was by far the worst part.', "Giants and pit spawn attempted to topple the cathedral's pillars. The fine grit of their remains still swirls in the breeze outside.", 'Gisela cornered the murderous demon among the graves of the dead villagers. "A fitting end," she murmured as she raised her sword.', 'Goblins were first to see the potential of hedrons in the fight against the Eldrazi, for the magical stones came ready-made with pointy bits.', "Goblins' eager curiosity leads them to scavenging, petty theft, and the rigging of sleek pirate ships. Some stop at scavenging.", "Goblins' fearlessness and diminutive size make them the perfect cannoneers.", 'Gront realized that his brilliant plan of being faster than Kork might still not be enough.', 'Half a brain rules the mindless.', "Havengul wakes are widely regarded as great entertainment. If you're lucky, the guest of honor climbs out of the casket and joins in the festivities.", 'He never wastes energy distinguishing between friend and foe.', 'He only paused to catch his breath, not knowing that it would be his last.', "He vowed he would never rest until he reached his destination. He doesn't know how right he was.", 'Her song plucks the strings of the storm, shifting wind and storm into a harmony that will carry her ship to safety.', 'His kind were once hunted to near-extinction. Now, under his protection, they rule the savannah.', 'His sword sounded like a silver chime on the glass jar, and the sprite laughed with delight.', "History may be written by the triumphant, but it's often rewritten by the troublesome.", 'If only every message were as perfect as its bearer.', "If you feel the ground quake, run. If you hear its bellow, flee. If you see its teeth, it's too late.", 'Imagine a thousand tiny mushrooms cropping up within your lungs.', 'Immolation is the sincerest form of flattery.', 'Imprisonment teaches revenge. Hobbling teaches resignation.', 'In a Multiverse of endless possibilities, Aminatou decided to experience all of them.', 'In a culture of beauty, the most beautiful are worshipped as gods.', 'In dark times, Truth bears a blade.', 'In every swirl of the tide, it sees the awakening of things yet to come.', 'In his hands, the wind can become a weapon or a means of escape.', "In his hunger for power and knowledge, Urza dug deep into Dominaria's ancient past.", "In the hold of the *Heart of Kiran*, Chandra answered Dovin Baan's sabotage with an explosive retort.", 'In the silence of the ice, even dreams become still.', 'In times of peril, the vision the ancient paruns had for their city comes into focus.', 'Initiates need worry only about the trials. Everything else is in the hands of the gods.', 'Inspired by industrious silkworms, its maker crafted it to restore the broken pieces of the world.', 'Interlopers in Sultai territory usually end up as crocodile chow or baboon bait.', 'It beckons silently, waiting in the darkness.', 'It began as a flavor on the tongue, like a bloody morsel of roast boar—but soon the power was a conflagration in her veins.', "It carries the hopes of Zendikar's embattled wilds on its mighty boughs.", 'It formed a friendship with several playful spirits, and soon "the pack" was known as the source of much mischief in Eiganjo.', 'It glides around the city, a sublime combination of elegance and utility.', 'It herds souls toward eternal torment.', 'It manifests at wizard academies to siphon inspiration from young prodigies.', 'It sees itself in all of its creations.', 'It shreds its prey as each head fights for the choicest bits.', 'It slithers through the senses, constricting consciousness and poisoning perceptions.', "It took the Rimewind cultists days to realize they had successfully activated the creature—it just wasn't interested in moving.", 'It was the perfect disguise—at least until its stomach started moaning.', "It wasn't the first time the dragon's hoard had attracted a free lunch.", 'It withers fruit and flesh alike.', "It's a small step from revel to bloodbath.", "It's bad luck to step on one, but worse luck to have one step on you.", "It's easy to be two steps ahead when you can see their every thought.", "It's often mistaken for the coming dawn as it gallops across the horizon.", 'Its assistance is unnervingly similar to its hunting technique.', 'Its collection is vast, yet each ship has a special place in its heart.', 'Its ferocity is tempered by patience, knowing it must wait for just the right moment to strike a killing blow.', 'Its insatiable hunger quickly depletes a region of prey. It must migrate from place to place to feed its massive bulk.', 'Its last life is spent tormenting your dreams.', 'Its spark is worse than its bite.', 'Its teeth exist only for decoration.', 'Keeping the streets of the Sixth District safe, one escaped Simic mutant at a time.', "Keldon raiders' spoils are limited to what their colos can carry. No matter the value, the rest goes up in smoke.", 'Kidnappers caught in Havengul are given two choices: languish in prison or become rat catchers. The smart ones go to prison.', 'Kitesailing is a way of life—and without practice, the end of it.', 'Knowledge demands sacrifice.', "Lavabrink's boiling moat is a deterrent for most, and a relaxing bath for one.", 'Leonin claws were already deadly weapons of natural evolution before he improved upon them.', 'Light streaked down from the heavens, and a voice whispered in the soldier\'s ear: "You shall not fall today."', "Linger on death's door and risk being invited in.", "Lukka's bond provided not only friendship, but also the most powerful weapon in his arsenal.", 'Lumengrid, site of the Knowledge Pool, source of vedalken arcana.', "Made in its creator's image, though slightly more clangy.", 'Maintaining a personal bubble is even more important when you have gills.', 'Many a besieged city has surrendered upon hearing the distinctive rumble of the juggernaut.', 'Many deaths are distasteful, but only a few are truly repugnant.', 'May the worthy spend an eternity in Blessed Sleep. May the wicked find the peace of oblivion.', 'Memories of ages past are said to swim the minds of lounging fallowsages.', 'Most goblins get their turn firing the catapult, but few achieve the coveted title of Ammunition Holder.', 'Most smiths shape metal, but some prefer more delicate materials.', 'Naturally inquisitive and adaptable, goblins can turn their small stature to their advantage as rogues.', 'Neurok spies carry devices that let them look a few moments into the future, giving them an almost insurmountable edge.', 'Nirkana assassins craft incurable concoctions by mixing basilisk marrow and deathwillow sap with the vital fluids of a dozen other poisonous species.', 'No battle means more to a Mardu warrior than the one that earns her war name.', 'No part goes to waste.', 'No ripples, no splashes, no warning.', 'No weapon stays on the rack for long in the Burning Yard.', 'Not all heroes die in armor.', 'Not since the days of Pashalik Mons have the Rundvelt goblins been so united or effective.', 'Nothing is wasted on New Phyrexia.', "Nothing quickens the predator's blood like the unfamiliar scents of new hunting grounds and the mewling cries of new prey.", 'Nothing stops industry in Ravnica—certainly not the safety of its workers.', "Oketra's closest viziers are known as her chosen, though others may have a better claim to that moniker.", 'On Ikoria, reactive magic can make the difference between barely grazed and really dead.', 'On occasion, felidars leave meaty "gifts" outside the tents of explorers they consider worthy.', 'On still nights you can hear its rotted teeth grinding tirelessly on scavenged bones.', 'Once he gets up and going, he will forever shamble on.', 'One way to keep the peace is to make war look like a really bad idea.', 'Only an imitation of tortured shrieking\\n—or so the Rakdos claim.', "Outside Drannith's walls, where collateral damage is of no concern, the Coppercoats are free to use more potent methods.", 'Palmistry is much more effective when you read the fine print.', 'Part feline, part primate, all trouble.', 'Perfect for keeping time at a battle or a ball.', 'Reflections from the wind-sculpted snow gleam with every color of the rainbow.', 'Remarkably, dinner continued with no further interruptions.', "Renegades find ever more creative ways to work around the Consulate's aether regulations.", 'Riding the goat\\n—Dwarven expression meaning\\n"a foolhardy act of bravery"', 'Rootha created constantly, passionately, in hopes of impressing her greatest critic: herself.', 'Scarecrows only go so far in sending the message to stay away.', 'Scholars had puzzled for centuries over the ruins at Tal Terig. Its secrets had always lived within one rune-carved head.', "Serum was once derived from Mirrodin's blinkmoths, offering visions of inspiration. Now it is pulled from Phyrexian inkmoths, yielding visions of perfection.", 'Servants at Vess Manor are chosen for their strong work ethic and respectful demeanor. Being alive is not required.', 'She endures without Avacyn but secretly asks each soul she guides if they have seen her.', 'She had always believed in the transformative powers of great literature.', 'She never would\'ve guessed that her last word would be "Whoops!"', 'She wails for those who have died, and for those who are about to.', "Shintan sensed the malice in his opponent, but he did not strike until the orc's muscles tensed in preparation to throw the first punch.", 'Sky pirates often leap randomly into the fray and assume there will be something to land on.', "Slonk was struck by lightning twenty-seven times before he got the idea. Another forty-three hits and he'd perfected it.", 'Some Golgari insects live for centuries—and they never stop growing.', 'Some Ravnicans consider carrying a sword to be beneath them, preferring instead a tooth-and-claw escort.', 'Some druids nurture gardens. Others nurture continents.', 'Some heroes line their coats with yeti fur. More yetis line their bellies with heroes.', "Some say the valley of Glen Elendra is mythical, and that rumors of its existence are nothing but a faerie prank. Others say it is the fae's most fiercely guarded secret.", 'Some spirits cling to one person, feasting on the growing fear until a final moment of all-consuming terror.', 'Some took to their boats to escape the unfolding nightmare. The remains of their vessels now litter the shores of Nephalia.', 'Some will sacrifice everything for but a taste of power.', 'Sometimes knowledge takes on a life of its own.', 'Sometimes the greatest strength is the strength of conviction.', 'Sometimes the weight of the world on your shoulders is a literal one.', "Sometimes you die a glorious death with your sword held high. Sometimes you're just target practice.", 'Sparkmages are performance artists of sorts, but pain is the price of admission.', 'Spirits disturbed by ghoulcallers become geists driven by restless anger.', 'Starfish are its favorite prey.', "Taborax's cultists are the latest in a long history of beings who have desired to see Zendikar torn to pieces.", "Teferi's legacy lives on in Tolaria through the study of time magic and a tradition of irrepressible mischief.", "The Boros built a prison in the sky where Azorius statutes couldn't restrict their sense of justice.", 'The Consulate keeps watch at each of the eleven bridges to ensure that the market remains a haven for commerce, not for con artists.', 'The River Heralds would wreck a thousand ships to keep intruders from finding the golden city.', 'The Skelle raise scorn poles in conquered villages—cursed totems of wood and bone that sap survivors of physical strength and the will to fight back.', "The Street Swarm is the labor class that drives the Golgari's endless cycle of life and death.", "The Ulvenwald makes no allowances for youth. Today's newborn is either tomorrow's hunter or tomorrow's lunch.", 'The apes of Yavimaya draw strength from the spirits of their ancestors.', 'The artificers of Kaladesh strive ceaselessly for perfection, progress, and the ultimate expression of elegance.', 'The assassins of the Ochran distill toxins from the remains of their previous victims.', 'The battle served as a grim reminder of what a final victory for the Eldrazi would mean.', 'The best recipes start with reliable cookware.', 'The best swords are forged with dragonfire.', 'The blacksmith forgot to feed the forge, so the forge fed itself.', "The castle's mages had devised effective counters to every form of siegecraft, but had no answers to gorilla warfare.", 'The daredevil racers of the Derby Crows, long at odds with the Consulate, were quick to join the renegades in open revolt.', 'The demons took no captives and claimed no spoils; they sought only to destroy.', 'The devil appreciated the irony of using doves for ammunition. The townsfolk, not so much.', 'The drive to hunt and feed is raw instinct for dinosaurs. The trick is simply to channel it in the right direction.', 'The dwarves believe works of art should be passed down the generations, not buried with the dead.', 'The efreet are drawn to the Kaisham Wanderers, a loosely organized Jeskai school where trickery is employed to challenge the status quo and upend the belief systems of others.', "The elves had devised countless strategies to combat Memnarch's war machines, but they had no idea what to do when one was *thrown* at them.", 'The experiments decided to perform some research of their own.', "The fae know when they're not wanted. That's precisely why they show up.", 'The first spell taught to young mages, it has spared the lives of many whose hands are too small to hold a sword.', 'The flesh is dead and the life forgotten, but old habits persist.', 'The folk of Kessig build up their courage by burning effigies of the things they fear.', 'The goblins made an unruly pile with military precision.', 'The greatest minds in Meletis study under the masters at the Dekatia, a renowned school of magic and philosophy.', 'The hatchlings will fill the jungles of Murasa in a glittering tide.', 'The hierarchy of the Uktabi Jungle hinges mostly on who can keep Prince Kibo entertained.', 'The hive has a long memory. It knows how every member ever died, and to whom it owes the grudge.', 'The hound sniffed the air and let slip a low growl. General Takeno looked down at the faithful Isamaru and calmed him with a touch. "Alert the guard. The kami are coming."', 'The hunt ends. Lunch begins.', 'The impact sent the soldiers scattering—then something came out of the crater.', 'The indigo dragon gladly traded a bit of its hoard for everlasting moonlight.', 'The insectile kraul lurk in the tunnels below street level. Many are loyal to the Golgari Swarm, but others follow their own esoteric caste system.', 'The kor send their thopter kites to see if the land is in a welcoming mood.', 'The might of an army with the restraint of a child.', 'The most successful entertainers on New Capenna feature an element of medium-to-extreme danger in their acts.', "The mushrooms growing in the wolves' fur possess curative properties incredible enough to tempt many alchemists into risking their lives to track one down.", 'The nightsong begins with a lone howl, but soon swells to a deafening chorus.', 'The oil sloshes against his skull as he nears his destination: the Frogtosser Games and the lighting of the Flaming Boggart.', 'The people of Tarkir speak of an ancient legend, of the dragon-man called Sarkhan who was greatest of all khans.', "The problem wasn't that fish had learned how to fly. It was that sharks had adapted to follow them.", 'The river is a powerful friend.', 'The scouring sands of Shefet polish its carapace, and the ranks of the cursed fill its belly.', 'The spirit cares nothing for the crimes or triumphs of the slain. It shelters all beneath its stormy cloak.', 'The staccato clatter of its metal claws on pavement is unmistakable.', 'The streets of Ravnica are full of former guild members now using their institutional skills for personal gain.', 'The strongest pack has the fiercest pups.', 'The tenderness of a mother. The pity of a mantis.', 'The thief doubled back twice, doused herself with perfume, crossed the ocean, and still woke up with her pursuer close on her heels.', 'The throng flitted from castle to castle, leaving a trail of star-crossed love, damaging rumors, and missing heirlooms in their wake.', 'The time for training was done. Only one final trial stood between Amin and his place among the honored dead.', "The upside to not thinking about the consequences is that you'll always surprise those who do.", 'The vedalken order their Neurok sentinels to watch over the shores of the Quicksilver Sea, as if they know of intruders yet to come.', 'The viziers serving Rhonas, the god of strength, maintain the menagerie of animals employed during his trial.', "The wastelands disorient even the most experienced scouts, making them easy prey for Kozilek's drones.", 'Their arrival is heralded by the deafening hum of ten thousand wings. Their departure is marked by the silence of the dead.', 'Their feeding habits leave them with gizzards full of tumbled gems.', 'There are no weapons allowed in the Biblioplex, but a clever mage is never truly defenseless.', 'There is a sanctuary that reveals itself only to those graced by the *eludha*—the mystical connection between bonder and monster.', "There is only one fate left to those banished from the God-Pharaoh's city.", "There's no prepared like overprepared.", "There's no stronger armor than the bravery of those beside you.", "Theros's human philosophers were at a marked disadvantage due to their need to pause for things like food or sleep.", 'They are the first to greet dissenters on their journey into exile.', 'They often perch on street lamps, causing the poles to buckle under their weight.', 'Those who are chosen do not doubt. Those who remain do not lament.', 'Those who die as heroes are permitted to dwell in Ilysia, a protected realm of the Underworld as tranquil and vibrant as the rest is bleak.', 'Those who raged most bitterly at the world in life are cursed to roam the nether realms in death.', 'Those whose lives were uninspired are doomed to the wretched tedium of Phylias in death.', 'Though imprisoned in Jaspera trees, the elvish gods known as the Einir still whisper through the ages.', 'Though she is rightly feared, there are relatively few tales of her deeds in battle, for few survive her raids.', 'Time rifts bring tunneling beasts of old into the hard, dry earth of the present. Most die there, trapped, but the mightiest burst through the surface.', 'To know the battlefield is to anticipate the enemy. To know the enemy is to anticipate victory.', 'To some satyrs, only blasphemy is sacred.', 'To thallids, the whole world is just a pile of mulch to grow saprolings in.', 'Trapped in Immersturm, it bloodies its blade not for ideals or territory or power, but simply to pass the time.', 'Trapped in a realm of dead flesh and scarce hunting, the ravenous wolves of Karfell follow the Dread Marn to warm game.', 'Trapped on Ravnica with no affection for either side, Ob Nixilis sought gratification in random acts of torment.', 'Tritons search for omens in its wake.', 'Two taken, two judged, one returned.', 'Urza studied the creations of the Thran not simply to learn from them, but to surpass them.', 'Urza threw himself into his research, pushing the boundaries of both possibility and morality.', "Vampires don't consider patience a virtue nor gluttony a sin.", 'Victims spirited through a faerie ring find themselves stranded miles away.', 'Visit the dead, and they may return the favor.', 'Vowing to free the souls of her children, Kastinne followed the tormentors into the ghastly network of caves below Stensia.', 'War begins with one red ember.', 'What the rangers thought were warning growls turned out to be nothing but monstrous snoring.', 'When Asha left Bant, she ensured that the world would have protection and order in her absence.', 'When Baral constructed his trap for Chandra, he did not account for the arrival of an enormous leonin wielding a twin-headed axe.', "When Belzenlok's lieutenant Yar-Kul grew too ambitious, the Demonlord transformed him into a maggot. The frog that ate the maggot grew and grew, until a ravenous spirit burst from its body.", 'When one leonin hunts, many more are surely nearby.', 'When they call, nature answers.', "When they had the house checked for bugs, they didn't think big enough.", 'When things get ugly above ground, goblins resort to alternate routes of passage.', 'Where she flies, the Light of Starnheim shines.', 'Where the light falls dim and blue on broken ships, secrets lie unclaimed.', 'While hunting aether, a gremlin may ignore other stimuli, including threats to its own life.', 'While the realm has laws, in the wilds there are other ways of balancing power.', 'Whoever wins, the neighborhood loses.', 'Wildflowers here bloom not with the season but with the ebb and flow of magic.', "With Thraben's army recalled to its city walls, outlying villages were left to fend for themselves.", "With fewer patrols about, Kessig's roads have become prime hunting grounds.", 'With the Hekma destroyed, the wandering dead that sought entrance to Naktamun had free rein to lay waste to the city.', "With the new guildmaster's innovations, arresters can arrive on the scene moments before a crime is committed.", "With their factories long destroyed, some of Mishra's creations still toil in remote areas, endlessly performing and reperforming their last orders.", 'With their usual prey scared off by werewolves, the wolves of the Ulvenwald adopted inventive new hunting techniques.', 'Wolves that feast on zombie flesh and survive carry the foul diseases of the dead wherever they roam.', 'You can gather a tidy fortune if you can avoid getting clobbered by falling treasure.', "You don't so much hire goblins as put ideas in their heads.", "You don't want to know how she got that name.", "You know you've ventured too deep when the rats stop running and hold their ground.", 'Young artificers on Kaladesh let their imaginations run wild.']
